Every integer $n>1$ is a product of primes, uniquely up to order. Existence follows by <strong induction>: if $n$ is not prime, factor it into smaller positive integers and apply induction. For uniqueness, if
$$p_1\cdots p_r=q_1\cdots q_s,$$
Euclid's lemma makes $p_1$ divide some $q_j$, hence equal it. Cancel that prime and induct on the number of factors.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

